== 1. K-1 P5: the six-pointed star and the three lines need the Problem 4 restart
   6 dots, hop 1, hopping from the black dot until back (Problems 1-3, 6-7): [(0, 1), (0, 5), (1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4), (4, 5)]; = printed star: False; = printed three lines: False
   6 dots, hop 2, hopping from the black dot until back (Problems 1-3, 6-7): [(0, 2), (0, 4), (2, 4)]; = printed star: False; = printed three lines: False
   6 dots, hop 3, hopping from the black dot until back (Problems 1-3, 6-7): [(0, 3)]; = printed star: False; = printed three lines: False
   6 dots, hop 4, hopping from the black dot until back (Problems 1-3, 6-7): [(0, 2), (0, 4), (2, 4)]; = printed star: False; = printed three lines: False
   6 dots, hop 5, hopping from the black dot until back (Problems 1-3, 6-7): [(0, 1), (0, 5), (1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4), (4, 5)]; = printed star: False; = printed three lines: False
   with restarts (Problem 4): hop 2 -> [(0, 2), (0, 4), (1, 3), (1, 5), (2, 4), (3, 5)], hop 3 -> [(0, 3), (1, 4), (2, 5)]

== 2. K-1 guide: "Lands on every dot" means every dot gets a marker before the counter is back
   4 dots: hop -> (every dot marked, every other dot marked): {1: (False, True), 2: (False, False), 3: (False, True)}
   5 dots: hop -> (every dot marked, every other dot marked): {1: (False, True), 2: (False, True), 3: (False, True)}
   6 dots: hop -> (every dot marked, every other dot marked): {1: (False, True), 2: (False, False), 3: (False, False)}
   7 dots: hop -> (every dot marked, every other dot marked): {1: (False, True), 2: (False, True), 3: (False, True), 4: (False, True), 5: (False, True), 6: (False, True)}

== 3. 4-5 P12 / guide: "a dot that lands on itself gets no line"
   x2: dot 0 lands on itself, yet the lines from dots [12] end at dot 0
   x3: dot 0 lands on itself, yet the lines from dots [8, 16] end at dot 0
   x3: dot 12 lands on itself, yet the lines from dots [4, 20] end at dot 12

== 4. Guide P12 and section 5: where the dents (cusps) of the times-table pictures are
   x2: chords passing within 0.08 R of 1/3 of the way to dot 12: 7 (not counting chords that merely end there: 7)
   x2: chords passing within 0.08 R of dot 0: 3 (not counting chords that merely end there: 2)
   x2: envelope touches the dot circle at the self-landing dots [0]
   x3: chords passing within 0.08 R of 1/2 of the way to dot 6: 5 (not counting chords that merely end there: 5)
   x3: chords passing within 0.08 R of 1/2 of the way to dot 18: 5 (not counting chords that merely end there: 5)
   x3: chords passing within 0.08 R of dot 0: 2 (not counting chords that merely end there: 0)
   x3: chords passing within 0.08 R of dot 12: 2 (not counting chords that merely end there: 0)
   x3: envelope touches the dot circle at the self-landing dots [0, 12]

== 5. K-1 P8: rows needed before the top row comes back with hop 2 on 6 pictures: 3 (5 blank rows printed)

== 6. Guide materials: "Coloured pencils, 6+ colours ... a new colour for each start"
   K-1: most starts on any ring a child draws = 3
   2-3: most starts on any ring a child draws = 6
   4-5: most starts on any ring a child draws = 6
